@startuml sequence-pdf-range-streaming
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: one open of a PDF in the viewer is one counted GET and many uncounted
'       ranges; the first GET renders the reader's copy (from a shared base
'       a worker built after the file's first reader) and pins it; every
'       range after it reads the pin and is cut from that one stored copy,
'       by Django or (optionally) by nginx.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, catalog code (issue 214). Scope: user-acquisition
'       download. Omitted: base64 format, anonymous shared copies, errors.
' Source: apps/files/views.py (UserAcquisitionDownload), apps/files/ranges.py,
'         apps/files/personalised.py, apps/files/signing.py,
'         apps/core/modifiers/pdf/__init__.py, apps/tasks/tasks.py,
'         docs/files/streaming.md (2026-11-18).
' =============================================================================

title PDF range streaming: count once, render once, pin, cut ranges (issue 214, 2026-11-18)

actor "Reader" as reader
participant "Portal ·\npdf.js" as viewer
participant "Catalog API\n(gunicorn)" as api
database "Redis cache" as cache
database "Storage\n(NFS / S3)" as storage
participant "Celery worker" as worker
participant "nginx\n(optional)" as nginx <<proposed>>

reader -> viewer : open book
viewer -> api : POST /api/v1/user-acquisitions
api --> viewer : 201 { url, <b>stream_url</b> (?exp&sig), stream_url_expires_at }

== first request: GET without Range (counted) ==
viewer -> api : GET stream_url
api -> api : verify sig → owner; IP block; permission
api -> api : popularity + 1 (one UPDATE), activity, read
api -> cache : ready marker of copy?
alt copy missing
  api -> cache : lock copy
  api -> cache : ready marker of the file's base?
  alt base ready
    api -[$accent_msg()]> storage : <b>render copy from base</b> (licence page, QR, annotations;\n<b>garbage=1, deflate, objstms</b>) → personalised/<ua>/<digest>.pdf
  else first reader of the file
    api -> worker : queue build_personalised_base (once per file)
    api -> storage : render copy from source in full (as before)
  end
  api -> cache : ready marker, unlock
end
worker -> storage : normalise source once (garbage=4, clean, deflate, objstms)\n→ personalised/_base/ (no reader data)
worker -> cache : base ready marker (7 days after last use)
api -> cache : pin (name, size, ETag, Last-Modified), 15 min
api --> viewer : 200, Accept-Ranges, Content-Length,\nstrong ETag (hash of name, size, mtime), Last-Modified
viewer -> viewer : abort body after headers

== every range after it (never counted) ==
loop pages drawn
  viewer -> api : GET stream_url, Range: bytes=a-b
  api -> api : verify sig; IP block; permission
  api -> cache : read pin (+ touch copy marker)
  alt Django path (default)
    api -> storage : read bytes a..b of the copy
    api --> viewer : 206, Content-Range, ETag
  else EVILFLOWERS_FILES_ACCEL (filesystem storage)
    api --> nginx : 200, X-Accel-Redirect: /_files/personalised/…
    nginx -> storage : sendfile a..b
    nginx --> viewer : 206, Content-Range (CORS re-added)
  end
end

caption A range never recomputes the copy: the pin holds its name and validators, and the copy's marker keeps it from idling out.\nThe base holds no reader data and is shared by every reader of the file; the copy is one revision, so no clean source sits inside it.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/sequence-pdf-range-streaming.puml
@enduml
